<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gattilusio</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Gattilusio family</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Gattilusio were a Genoese family who ruled the island of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lesbos">Lesbos</a> and other northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegean">Aegean</a> territories from 1355 to 1462. Their power began when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francesco-i-gattilusio">Francesco I Gattilusio</a> helped Emperor John V Palaiologos regain his throne and received Lesbos as a dowry. Branches later held Ainos, Thasos, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samothrace">Samothrace</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lemnos">Lemnos</a> and Old <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phocaea">Phocaea</a> as Byzantine and then Ottoman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a>, until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mehmed-ii">Mehmed II</a> conquered their lands.</p></div>
